{
  "configuration_id": "config_034",
  "reason": "Evidence: config_007 (multimodal, pca_n2000, resnet50, weighted) achieves 0.5232 acc, while RNA-only pca_n2000 (config_019) achieves 0.4849 and image-only resnet50 (config_002) only 0.2079. RNA is clearly the dominant signal, and the multimodal gain over RNA-only is modest (+0.038). The only RNA encoder tested so far is pca_n2000, a simple linear projection. Uncertainty: whether a learned, generative RNA representation (scgpt) meaningfully improves the dominant modality's contribution. This experiment (config_034) changes exactly one factor from config_007—RNA encoder from pca_n2000 to scgpt—while holding image encoder (resnet50), profile (single), and fusion (weighted) constant. If scgpt substantially outperforms pca_n2000, it tells us to invest in richer RNA representations as the highest-leverage design choice; if not, it confirms pca_n2000 is near-sufficient and redirects budget toward multiprofile or image-encoder improvements. This is the most informative single-factor test under the limited budget because it isolates the effect on the modality that carries most of the signal."
}

